cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  ctdose-core: open, auditable CT dose surveillance from DICOM, with a physics
  reconstruction when the dose attributes are missing
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this file) and the
  paper describing it, listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yamamoto
    given-names: Shuji
    email: yamamoto@lisit.jp
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9211-1071'
    affiliation: Institute of One, LISIT Co., Ltd., Tokyo 150-0044, Japan
repository-code: https://github.com/Institute-of-One/ctdose-core
url: https://github.com/Institute-of-One/ctdose-core
abstract: >-
  A Python package that computes CTDIvol, dose-length product, size-specific dose
  estimate and effective dose from CT DICOM data. It reads a recorded dose where
  one exists -- from a CT Radiation Dose Structured Report or the image header --
  and reconstructs one from acquisition physics where none does, which is the
  common case in public imaging archives. Every value carries its formula, its
  inputs and its provenance, so recorded and reconstructed figures never become
  interchangeable by accident.
keywords:
  - computed tomography
  - radiation dose
  - CTDIvol
  - size-specific dose estimate
  - DICOM
  - radiation dose structured report
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
# Set to the tag date when the release is cut; Zenodo takes the date from the
# GitHub release, so this is the human-readable copy rather than the authority.
date-released: '2026-11-09'
# The *concept* DOI: it resolves to the latest version, which is what a citation of
# the project should point at. The manuscript's data-availability statement cites the
# *version* DOI instead, so the paper names the exact snapshot it was run on.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21636082
references:
  - type: data
    title: Low Dose CT Image and Projection Data
    doi: 10.7937/9npb-2637
    notes: >-
      The public TCIA collection used for the demonstration figures. No imaging from
      it is redistributed with this software; see docs/REPRODUCING_FIGURES.md.
    authors:
      - family-names: Moen
        given-names: Taylor R.
      - family-names: Chen
        given-names: Baiyu
      - family-names: Holmes
        given-names: David R.
        name-suffix: III
      - family-names: McCollough
        given-names: Cynthia H.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    An open-source, provenance-aware framework for reconstructing missing CT dose
    indices from DICOM metadata
  authors:
    - family-names: Yamamoto
      given-names: Shuji
      orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9211-1071'
      affiliation: Institute of One, LISIT Co., Ltd., Tokyo 150-0044, Japan
  journal: Journal of Applied Clinical Medical Physics
  year: 2026
  # DOI is assigned at acceptance; until then this entry names the manuscript
  # rather than a published article, and must not be cited as if it were one.
  status: submitted
